 {"type": "ellipse", "id": "same", "x": 850, "y": 1005, "w": 160, "h": 70, "stroke": "#047857", "fill": "#a7f3d0"},
 {"type": "text", "id": "samet", "x": 930, "y": 1022, "fs": 14, "stroke": "#374151", "align": "center",
  "text": "same as\none run? yes"},
 {"type": "arrow", "id": "a_glue_same", "x": 812, "y": 1040, "points": [[0, 0], [36, 0]], "stroke": "#1e3a5f"},
 {"type": "text", "id": "sortt", "x": 390, "y": 1124, "fs": 14, "stroke": "#374151",
  "text": "For sort it went further and wrote the step that\nmerges sorted pieces back together. The paper puts\nthat step outside Caruca's scope."},

 {"type": "text", "id": "badh", "x": 1080, "y": 919, "fs": 16, "stroke": "#b91c1c",
  "text": "A poor judge of its own work"},
 {"type": "rectangle", "id": "la", "x": 1080, "y": 965, "w": 190, "h": 50, "stroke": "#6d28d9", "fill": "#ddd6fe"},
 {"type": "text", "id": "lat", "x": 1175, "y": 981, "fs": 14, "stroke": "#374151", "align": "center", "text": "writes its files"},
 {"type": "rectangle", "id": "lb", "x": 1330, "y": 965, "w": 210, "h": 50, "stroke": "#6d28d9", "fill": "#ddd6fe"},
 {"type": "text", "id": "lbt", "x": 1435, "y": 972, "fs": 14, "stroke": "#374151", "align": "center",
  "text": "tests them against\nits own stand-in"},
 {"type": "ellipse", "id": "lc", "x": 1195, "y": 1050, "w": 230, "h": 56, "stroke": "#047857", "fill": "#a7f3d0"},
 {"type": "text", "id": "lct", "x": 1310, "y": 1068, "fs": 15, "stroke": "#374151", "align": "center", "text": "\"all passed\""},
 {"type": "arrow", "id": "l_ab", "x": 1272, "y": 990, "points": [[0, 0], [56, 0]], "stroke": "#6d28d9"},
 {"type": "arrow", "id": "l_bc", "x": 1430, "y": 1017, "points": [[0, 0], [-35, 36]], "stroke": "#6d28d9"},
 {"type": "arrow", "id": "l_ca", "x": 1222, "y": 1056, "points": [[0, 0], [-40, -39]], "stroke": "#047857"},
 {"type": "rectangle", "id": "real", "x": 1580, "y": 965, "w": 150, "h": 50, "stroke": "#c2410c", "fill": "#fed7aa"},
 {"type": "text", "id": "realt", "x": 1655, "y": 972, "fs": 14, "stroke": "#374151", "align": "center",
  "text": "the real PaSh\nprogram"},
 {"type": "arrow", "id": "a_real", "x": 1542, "y": 990, "points": [[0, 0], [36, 0]], "stroke": "#b91c1c", "style": "dashed"},
 {"type": "text", "id": "realr", "x": 1580, "y": 1027, "fs": 13, "stroke": "#b91c1c",
  "text": "sort: no answer,\nand the error\nis hidden"},
 {"type": "text", "id": "bullets", "x": 1080, "y": 1124, "fs": 14, "stroke": "#374151",
  "text": "- In all 6 runs its report claimed more testing\n  than its logs show\n- binwalk: ran 16 of 51 options; never mentioned\n  -D, which makes binwalk run other programs\n- Little isolation: even rm ran in one scratch folder"},

 {"type": "line", "id": "div3", "x": 40, "y": 1225, "points": [[0, 0], [1700, 0]], "stroke": "#64748b", "sw": 1, "style": "dashed"},

 {"type": "text", "id": "so", "x": 40, "y": 1243, "fs": 22, "stroke": "#1e40af", "text": "So what?"},
 {"type": "text", "id": "sot", "x": 390, "y": 1243, "fs": 16, "stroke": "#374151",
  "text": "Each is strong where the other is weak. The agent is good at finding things out (asking the command,\nwriting the merge step); Caruca is good at checking (sandbox, recorded file access, repeatable runs)."},
 {"type": "text", "id": "fine", "x": 40, "y": 1305, "fs": 13, "stroke": "#64748b",
  "text": "Each command ran once, with one prompt, and no syntax file has been scored yet: these are case studies, not rates. Runs 4 to 9, October 2026, Claude Fable 5.1 at medium effort, no web access.\nRow 2 counts come from Caruca's own command-line generator fed each syntax file (2026-10-20): convert at its default settings, cut at up to 4 options per line."}
]
